<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 Unit 4 Lesson 5 Write Division Expressions"><h2>Number Talk — equal differences</h2><p>225−100 = 227−102 = 230−105 = 220−95 = <strong>125</strong>. Discuss why increasing or decreasing BOTH numbers by the same amount keeps their difference.</p>
<h2>Bug card sort — six independently modelled 2021 situations</h2><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Card</th><th>Expression</th><th>Answer</th><th>Unknown</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A: Mole crickets</td><td>10÷5</td><td>2</td><td>Items per animal</td></tr><tr><td>B: Beetles</td><td>8÷2</td><td>4</td><td>Number of animals</td></tr><tr><td>C: Bees</td><td>14÷2</td><td>7</td><td>Number of animals</td></tr><tr><td>D: Dragonflies</td><td>12÷4</td><td>3</td><td>Number of animals</td></tr><tr><td>E: Ants</td><td>30÷5</td><td>6</td><td>Items per animal</td></tr><tr><td>F: Butterflies</td><td>50÷5</td><td>10</td><td>Items per animal</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Classify <strong>A, E and F</strong> as group-size problems and <strong>B, C and D</strong> as group-count problems. Teacher checks justification and original card sort. Original insect photo and publisher blackline card artwork are not embedded.</p>
